{"title":"Career Roadmap · Energy Auditor","role":"Energy Auditor","summary":"An Energy Auditor evaluates how energy is consumed within buildings, industrial facilities, commercial establishments, and infrastructure, then identifies opportunities to reduce energy consumption, operating costs, and emissions without compromising production or comfort.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Energy / Renewable Energy Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Energy Auditor evaluates how energy is consumed within buildings, industrial facilities, commercial establishments, and infrastructure, then identifies opportunities to reduce energy consumption, operating costs, and emissions without compromising production or comfort."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Energy engineering"},{"text":"Electrical and thermal systems"},{"text":"Energy efficiency"},{"text":"Renewable energy"},{"text":"Industrial processes"},{"text":"HVAC systems"},{"text":"Utilities"},{"text":"Energy measurement"},{"text":"Data analytics"},{"text":"Financial analysis"},{"text":"Sustainability"},{"text":"Energy management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A graduate can enter through roles such as Energy Engineer, Energy Analyst, Energy Management Engineer, Sustainability Analyst, or Energy Audit Engineer. Senior energy-audit and statutory-auditor roles may require specific professional credentials and eligibility under applicable regulations."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"note","label":"2026–2030","text":"Energy Engineering Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build practical capability in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Energy consumption analysis"},{"text":"Electrical systems"},{"text":"Thermal systems"},{"text":"HVAC"},{"text":"Motors and pumps"},{"text":"Boilers"},{"text":"Compressed air"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"En